    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22201" root="شرق" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرِيقٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرْقٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also A boy, or young man,
<i>goodly,</i> or <i>beautiful,</i> (K, TA,) <i>in face:</i> (TA:)
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُرُقٌ</span>, (K, TA, [in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرْقٌ</span>, but correctly])
with two dammehs. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And A woman
<i>small in the vulva:</i> (Ibn-'Abbád, O, K:) or
<i>having her vagina and rectum united by the
rending of the separation between them;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفْضَاةٌ</span>. (M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشَّرِيقُ</span> is the name of
<i>A certain idol.</i> (M, TA.)

